                "content": "<p>In Indian universities, faculty often distribute a single, generalized study guide to a class of 500 students before final exams. This one-size-fits-all approach is deeply inefficient.</p>\n<p>A top-performing student might waste hours re-reading basic definitions they already mastered, while a struggling student might completely miss that their core weakness is in higher-order application questions. Faculty simply lack the time to manually analyze 500 individual exam histories and write 500 bespoke study plans.</p>\n<p>By deploying a centralized university assessment platform, institutions can automatically map historical student performance data directly to targeted revision materials, bridging the gap between assessment and actual learning.</p>"
